  "result": "Perfect! All 158 tests pass. I've successfully implemented payment terms support:\n\n**Updated `src/errors.js`:**\n- Added `TERMS_INVALID`: \"Payment terms must be NET14, NET30, or EOM.\"\n\n**Updated `src/dates.js`** with helper functions:\n- `lastDayOfMonth(date)` \u2014 returns the last day of the month for a given date\n  - Correctly handles all month lengths\n  - Handles leap years for February\n\n- `calculateDueDate(issueDate, terms)` \u2014 calculates due date based on payment terms\n  - NET14: adds 14 days to issue date\n  - NET30: adds 30 days to issue date\n  - EOM: returns the last day of the issue date's month\n\n**Updated `src/invoices.js`:**\n- `createInvoice` now accepts optional `terms` parameter (defaults to 'NET30')\n- Validates terms (only 'NET14', 'NET30', 'EOM' allowed)\n- Calculates and stores `dueDate` on invoice\n- Stores `terms` on invoice\n- Returns TERMS_INVALID for unknown terms\n\n**Added 9 tests** covering:\n- Default NET30 terms and correct due date calculation\n- NET14 terms (14 days from issue)\n- NET30 terms explicitly specified\n- EOM (End of Month) terms\n- Invalid terms rejection\n- EOM with different month lengths:\n  - January (31 days)\n  - February in leap year (29 days)\n  - February in non-leap year (28 days)\n- NET14 at month boundaries (Dec 31 \u2192 Jan 14)\n\nAll 158 tests pass (149 previous + 9 new). Payment terms are now fully integrated into invoice creation.",
